    Suppose $\varphi\colon \A\to\A^*$ is a primitive substitution of length $k\geqslant 2$. Then, the following are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\ac(X_{\varphi})\in \{0,1\}$ (with $\ac(X_{\varphi})=0$ corresponding to $X_{\varphi}$ being  finite),
        \item $X_{\varphi}$ is null,
        \item $X_{\varphi}$ is tame.
