expanded_sketch:
The post-theorem introduction indicates the proof strategy for the main theorem as follows:
\begin{itemize}
\item Give an \emph{explicit strict presenter} of the intrinsically-defined global Stokes groupoid (defined as a $2$-fiber product): “provide an explicit small strict presenter for it, adapted to SNC depth and Kummer descent.”
\item “Construct a strict \v{C}ech--Stokes collar groupoid $\G_C$ and identify the correct collar moduli as $\operatorname{Sec}(\pi)$ (rather than $\Rep_r(\G_C)$), making the Stokes layer strictly functorial and cover-based.”
\item “Build the explicit $2$-pushout presenter $\G_{\Phi,n}$ and prove that it computes global Stokes objects via the torsorial gluing problem in establishing the main theorem.”
\item “Make the tame/Kummer layer along depth strata functorial at the level of presenters, enabling explicit descent constraints and, in particular, a hands-on description in terms of equivariant cocycles.”
\item Provide “finite skeletal models … and an explicit generators-and-relations/chamber-complex description in SNC corners,” i.e. an explicit coequalizer model for the presenter.
\end{itemize}

A more linear roadmap is also stated: “define the intrinsic groupoid $\Stokes_r(X^{\log}_n;D,\Phi)$ and establish its torsor description,” then “construct the interior \v{C}ech groupoid $\G_U$, the collar \v{C}ech--Stokes groupoid $\G_C$, and the overlap groupoid $\G_{\times}$, form the pushout
\begin{equation}\label{eq:pushout-intro}
\G_{\Phi,n}\ :=\ \GU \sqcup_{\GX} \GC.
\end{equation}
and prove the main theorem later.”

